{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012PC6gUkQntpVjfWUuAsQzs","type":"tool_result","content":"AUDIT_VERDICT: FAIL\nAUDIT_SUMMARY: The numbers, controls, comparators, qualification status and unscored-attempt handling all match the evidence, but two visible claims go beyond it: the SI says the agent wrote the evaluated finder, and the paper states as fact what the episode timings include.\nAUDIT_FINDING_COUNT: 2\nAUDIT_FINDING: id=finder-provenance-1 && section=Supplementary Information, LLM usage (paper.tex line 379); also Contributions (i) and Reproducibility record, Artifacts (line 374) || claim=An autonomous LLM-based research agent ... implemented the perturbation finder and the refined configurations || issue=The evidence shows the evaluated finder is the seeded starter baseline, not something the agent wrote. The text also says the three refined configurations were implemented, but they have no inspectable source and were never scored, so whether they were implemented cannot be checked. || evidence=paper_data.json downstream_study.selection_kind=baseline, source_attempt_id=bootstrap, source_program_dir=.baseline-seed-dewjjlsp/program_0, program_tree_sha256 equal to baseline_tree_sha256; source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py line 1 reads Starter perturbation finder and line 44 reads This starter: one-step influence (AMIP-style) ranking; program.py is byte-identical to source_evidence/downstream/baseline/src/program.py; study.attempts.scored=0 of total=3; paper.tex line 360 itself says no source for the refined configurations is among the artifacts || fix=In LLM usage, state that the evaluated finder is the provided starter/baseline configuration that was seeded before the search, and drop the claim that the agent implemented it. Say the three refined configurations were designed but have no inspectable source and were not scored. In Contributions (i) and the Artifacts paragraph, add that the finder is the baselin